<title>USA: Koch Oil raises U.S. posted crude prices 50 cts.</title>
<headline>Koch Oil raises U.S. posted crude prices 50 cts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Koch Oil said it had raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by 50 cents, effective Friday.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $18.75 a barrel and West Texas Sour to $16.00 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $18.25 and Oklahoma sweet is $18.75.</p>
<p>--New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859 1620</p>
</text>
